      "title": "Greeting at a lunch counter",
      "objective": "Greet staff politely at lunch, say your name, and recognize common lunch words in kana.",
      "focus": "こんにちは is a daytime greeting. すみません gets a server’s attention politely. は is pronounced wa in わたしは; です closes a polite statement. Katakana marks loanwords such as メニュー and ジュース.",
